# Build output
bin/
obj/
publish/

# IDE / editor
.vs/
.vscode/
.claude/
# Project-scoped skills + commands are checked in (they apply for every
# contributor); the shared settings.json (allowlist) is also checked in
# so every clone gets the same baseline. INVARIANTS.md and PR-AUDIT.md
# are durable architectural artifacts — they tell the story of how this
# repo is maintained. Everything else under .claude/ — runtime history,
# scheduled-task locks, per-user settings.local.json — stays ignored.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/commands/**
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/INVARIANTS.md
!.claude/PR-AUDIT.md
!.claude/README.md
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings.user
.idea/

# Data (Docker volume — not checked in)
# Exception: data/seeds/ is checked-in seed input (manifests consumed by
# CLI seeder commands, e.g. --seed-ingestion-sources reads
# data/seeds/ingestion_sources.v1.json). Runtime output (downloads,
# metadata, logs, snapshots, history) stays ignored.
# Exception: data/eval/ is checked-in eval ground-truth + committed
# results JSON per ADR-0016 — the metric trajectory is visible in
# `git log` so a prospect reviewing the repo sees the same trend a
# CI dashboard would.
# Exception: data/phase4/ is the Phase 4 curated-subset slate manifest
# per build-spec § Phase 4 scope item 7 — declarative documentation of
# the showcase's 7-machine intent set, consumed by
# tools/phase4/VerifyCuratedSubsetCoverage.csx.
# NOTE: pattern is `data/*` (not `data/`) so the parent isn't excluded —
# git can't re-include children whose parent directory is ignored.
data/*
!data/seeds/
!data/seeds/**
!data/eval/
!data/eval/**
!data/phase4/
!data/phase4/**

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Bicep — local parameter overrides (never committed; deploy script auto-detects)
*.local.bicepparam

# Bicep — generated ARM templates. Source of truth is the .bicep files;
# the compiled .json output is a build artifact (`az bicep build` /
# Deploy-SharedResources.ps1 emit it during validation/deploy).
infra/*.json
infra/**/*.json
infra/build/
infra/**/build/

# Operator-driven log outputs from manual H1/H2/H3 chain runs (Bicep
# apply, OPDB sync, recuration dry-runs, eval baseline runs, etc.).
# These are local diagnostic artifacts; the canonical results are the
# committed JSON files under data/eval/results/ per ADR-0016.
*.log

# Playwright responsive snapshot screenshots (written to ./screenshots/ by
# ResponsiveSnapshotTests during local test runs). In CI the screenshots/
# directory is captured as the `responsive-screenshots` artifact by the
# `snapshots` job — they are NOT committed to the repo.
screenshots/

# Cloudflare inventory — raw API dumps containing sensitive values
# (origin hostnames, cert fingerprints, error bodies). SUMMARY.md is
# the safe-to-share output; the JSON files are never committed.
cf-inventory/

# OpenTofu / Terraform local working artifacts. The provider mirror,
# crash logs, and saved plan files are machine-local: a plan (`tfplan`)
# contains the proposed state and may carry sensitive values — the
# README's "Things to avoid" section forbids committing it. The remote
# state lives in Azure Blob, so no local *.tfstate either.
#
# EXCEPTION: `.terraform.lock.hcl` is intentionally NOT ignored — it is
# the provider dependency lock and MUST be committed so CI and every
# developer resolve identical provider versions. Do not add it here.
.terraform/
*.tfplan
tfplan
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Agent worktree scratch — transient git worktrees created for isolated
# parallel agent runs. Never committed.
.worktrees/
